
 filluser - Fill or refresh records in the 'user' table from an Oracle source.

 Retrieves user information from the NCAR ORACLE server and inserts or
 updates records in the 'user' table of PostgreSQL database 'rdadb'.

 USAGE:
   filluser [-b] (-i | -n UserNumbers | -u UserLoginNames)

 OPTIONS (choose exactly one of -i, -n, or -u):

   -i   Refresh users that currently have incomplete information in the
        'user' table.

   -n UserNumbers
        Look up users by their NCAR system user numbers.

   -u UserLoginNames
        Look up users by their NCAR system login names.

   -b   Run in background mode (log to file only, no terminal output).

 EXAMPLE:
   filluser -u zji
